  <h2>Nature of the Service</h2>
  <p>
    Phronos is a cognitive research platform. Our instruments generate structured observations
    of cognition—what we call "telemetry." This telemetry serves two purposes: to provide you
    with insight into your own thinking patterns, and to contribute (with your consent) to a
    collective understanding of human cognition.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>You are a participant, not a user.</strong> A user consumes a product. A participant
    contributes to an endeavor. This distinction carries mutual obligation: we owe you transparency
    about how your data is used, clarity about what our instruments measure, and honesty about our
    limitations. You, in turn, engage with the understanding that your participation advances
    research beyond yourself.
  </p>

  <h2>What Phronos Is Not</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Phronos does not provide medical, psychological, therapeutic, or diagnostic services.</strong>
    Our instruments are research tools designed to generate observations about cognitive patterns.
    They are not validated clinical assessments, and their outputs do not constitute diagnoses,
    treatment recommendations, or professional advice of any kind.
  </p>
  <p>Specifically:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Instrument results (including "divergence" and "convergence" scores) reflect patterns in semantic associations. They do not measure intelligence, mental health status, cognitive impairment, or fitness for any purpose.</li>
    <li>Phronos instruments are not substitutes for evaluation by qualified healthcare professionals, psychologists, or psychiatrists.</li>
    <li>If you have concerns about your cognitive health, mental health, or psychological wellbeing, consult a licensed professional.</li>
    <li>Do not make medical, employment, educational, or legal decisions based on Phronos instrument results.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We disclaim all liability for decisions made in reliance on instrument outputs.</p>

  <h2>Eligibility</h2>
