  <h2>The INS-001 Instrument: Semantic Associations</h2>
  <p>INS-001 measures two dimensions of cognition:</p>
  <p>
    <strong>Divergence</strong> quantifies how far your semantic associations venture from
    statistically predictable paths. Higher divergence indicates more creative or unexpected
    conceptual connections.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Convergence</strong> quantifies how effectively your associations communicate
    meaning to others—specifically, whether an AI system can reconstruct your target word
    from your clues. Higher convergence indicates more effective encoding of semantic information.
  </p>
  <p>
    During the assessment, you provide a target word and five one-word association clues.
    These inputs are processed to generate your scores. The instrument takes approximately
    five minutes.
  </p>

